WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.147
Here is the workflow we will use throughout Module 6
First define

00:00:06.174 --> 00:00:11.755
the grain Ask what one output row should mean One
patient

00:00:12.676 --> 00:00:19.907
One admission One lab test One department Second

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:25.186
identify the two row sets you are combining Third
define the matching

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:29.475
rule Most often that is a key such as patient ID but

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:35.120
sometimes the relationship uses another identifier
Fourth decide

00:00:35.147 --> 00:00:39.873
which unmatched rows must remain If every patient
must remain even when

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:43.662
that patient has no admission that immediately
points toward a LEFT JOIN

00:00:43.689 --> 00:00:49.848
with patients on the left Fifth predict cardinality
Can

00:00:49.874 --> 00:00:55.387
one patient match several admissions Can one patient
also match several labs

00:00:56.308 --> 00:01:02.344
This prediction tells you whether rows may expand
Finally validate

00:01:03.254 --> 00:01:06.491
Compare the actual result with the number and type
of rows you

00:01:06.518 --> 00:01:11.570
expected This reasoning sequence is much safer than
starting by typing JOIN

00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:13.531
and hoping the result looks reasonable
